Patch series (third_party/patches/mewui/<category>/, applied in memory by vendor.py in the order the lock lists
them). A MANDATORY category cannot be skipped. Each header says what and why; hunks are the whole change.

  core-bridge (MANDATORY)
  0001-mewvg-context-app-branch.patch - Shared/Rendering/MewVG/MewVGGraphicsContext.Common.cs gains a
      `#elif MEWUI_MEWVG_MEWSTAGE` branch: the class MewStageMewVGGraphicsContext (with the dirty-rect interfaces
      and IGroupOpacityContext), `_vg` typed MewVGContext (the backend supplies a subclass over its own GPU device),
      and the GL-only clear / blit path compiled out so Clear() takes the fill path. Upstream branches unchanged.

  design-space (MANDATORY)
  0001-surface-scale-below-one.patch - a surface whose DPI scale is below 1 renders at that scale (it was clamped
      to 1, so an embedded host at 1280x720 showing a 1920x1080 design-space layout clipped a third of it).

  multi-host (MANDATORY: the test suites run several hosts in one process; secondary windows share a factory)
  0001-per-thread-ui-statics-and-graphics-factory.patch - VisualTree / LogicalTree traversal scratch is per
      thread and Application.ThreadGraphicsFactory (per thread) wins over the process-wide default factory, so
      several embedded hosts in one process (parallel test threads, or one after another) never share a traversal
      list or a text engine. Single-host behaviour unchanged.
  0002-per-thread-animation-manager.patch - AnimationManager is per UI thread (a clock keeps the manager it
      registered with), so one embedded host's per-frame pulse never ticks another host's transitions on the wrong
      thread. Single-UI-thread behaviour unchanged.
  0003-per-thread-dispatcher.patch - Application.ThreadDispatcher (per thread) is the dispatcher Window and
      DispatcherTimer use when no Application is running (Application.ResolveDispatcher). Without it an embedded
      host had none, so DispatcherTimer never ticked (caret blink, RepeatButton auto-repeat, the ScrollViewer idle
      timer, key-chord timeouts, toast expiry, long press) and BeginInvoke work never ran (deferred Tab focus into
      list rows, the hover re-check after a scroll). The backend binds a managed dispatcher it pumps once per
      frame. A running Application's dispatcher still wins: MewUI's own hosts are unchanged.

  allocation (optional; without it a steady-state UI frame allocates and the allocation gate tests fail)
  0001-replay-text-without-delegate.patch - RenderDataReplayer replays text by switching on the command kind
      instead of building a delegate per text command.
  0002-gradient-lut-identity-lookup.patch - NvgStrokeHelper's gradient LUT cache finds a stop list by reference
      first (ConditionalWeakTable), so a cached gradient needs no content key per draw.
  0003-resource-cache-evict-without-closure.patch - RenderResourceCache's budget eviction loops instead of
      running a LINQ lambda per frame.
  0004-scene-pass-without-per-frame-allocation.patch - the retained scene pass reuses its recorder, its dirty
      registry prunes in place, and the layer roots reuse the scene's array.
  0005-apply-template-without-per-call-closure.patch - Control.ApplyTemplate's presenter walk moved to its own
      method: the captured local made the compiler allocate a 32 B closure on EVERY call, and Window.PerformLayout
      calls it every frame.
  0006-dashed-stroke-without-per-draw-allocation.patch - NvgStrokeHelper (linked into MewStage.Ui.Backend) reuses
      per-thread scratch for software dashing instead of a new List and PathGeometry per dashed draw.

  text (optional)
  0001-letter-spacing-draws-per-grapheme.patch - letter-spaced text is drawn one grapheme per laid-out column, so
      the drawn glyphs sit where the layout put them (CSS letter-spacing); each grapheme's run box is at least its
      own advance, so a negative kerning pair does not cut the glyph on raster-box backends.
  0002-negative-half-leading.patch - a line box smaller than its text (CSS line-height below the font's) centres
      the text with negative half-leading, as CSS does; it was clamped at zero.

  rendering (optional)
  0001-rect-stroke-antialias-off-axis.patch - MewVG's rectangle stroke turns antialiasing off only on the pixel
      grid (as its rectangle fill does); a stroke under a skew came out stair-stepped.

  mewdock (optional; component mewdock, -p1 from extensions/MewUI.MewDock)
  0001-tool-caption-toggle.patch - DockingManager.ShowToolCaptions (default true) lets an app hide the tool-group
      caption bar when its panes carry their own header. Upstream behaviour with the default.

